                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "garybeihl",
                        "email": "garybeihl@microsoft.com",
                        "username": "garybeihl"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for finding and writing this up, binreaper. I ran into the same issue independently while reviewing bmcweb's HTTP/2 path and reproduced it end-to-end \u2014 an unauthenticated h2 stream with no Content-Length grows RSS roughly 1:1 until std::bad_alloc takes bmcweb down, while the HTTP/1.1 path returns 413 under the identical test. Your bytesReceived bound here is the right fix.\n\nThe only thing holding it up looks to be the CLA / legal-name requirement Ed noted. If that's a blocker on your end, I'm a CLA'd contributor and I'm glad to carry this forward under my sign-off \u2014 keeping you credited as the author/reporter and referencing this change. If you'd rather file the CLA and land it yourself, that's even better; just let me know how I can help.\n\nHappy to add the runtime-verification numbers as evidence either way \u2014 this is a real pre-auth DoS worth landing."
                }
            ],
